// ERROR-GOL-017 (GoL/HALLAZGOS.md) — a loop iterator over a name already in
// view writes that name. It is not a second variable.
//
// A block has no namespace of its own (PREMISES.md MEM-7), and every engine
// runs these loops by assigning the outer variable: after `@ m:1..3` the `m`
// of the file is 3. The analyser declared a new `m` for the loop instead, so
// the outer one was retired and reported `unused variable` while the program
// read it on the next line — and in the last case below, where the reads are
// inside the body, all three engines warned.
//
// This file's golden is its `check` output, and it must stay empty. The type
// change the same loop can make, which the analyser did not see either, is
// next door in iterador_cambia_el_tipo.zy.

m = 0
@ m:1..3 {
    >> m ¶
}
>> m ¶

s = "x"
@ s:["a", "b"] {
    >> s ¶
}
>> s ¶

k = 0
@ (k, v):[(1, 2), (3, 4)] {
    >> v ¶
}
>> k ¶

n = 0
@ n:[5, 6] {
    >> n ¶
}
